{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2866 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "83bae9d2351555752b515fc58f77240628a431cda9e51c4eb1f96c8f3a5b814d" :edb/db-before-t 2865 :edb/db-after-t 2866 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536178 50 #inst "2026-10-09T18:24:12.560Z" 13194139536178 true] [17592186198346 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387495 13194139536178 true] [17592186198346 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387502 13194139536178 true] [17592186198348 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387481 13194139536178 true] [17592186198348 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387488 13194139536178 true] [17592186198590 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536178 true] [17592186198590 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/assets/5b8ddb36e814517af21d790374e1fb192141bd6ef0fd99e83a147c6ed5a62aea.png)\n\nA plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ in the first quadrant bounded by the circles ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4,$ and the coordinate axes, as shown above. Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{3}{7}My.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." 13194139536178 true] [17592186198590 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4174/Source/Images/q-163586.png)\n\nA plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ in the first quadrant bounded by the circles $x^{2} + y^{2} = 1$, $x^{2} + y^{2} = 4$, and the coordinate axes, as shown above. Its mass density at any point is given by $λ(x, y) = \\frac{3}{7}My$. Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." 13194139536178 false] [17592186198590 1145 "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{3}{7}Mr\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M({\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}{r}^{5}{|}_{1}^{2}\\cdot {[-\\frac{{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta }{3}]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M\\cdot (\\frac{32}{5}-\\frac{1}{5})\\cdot (-0+\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M\\cdot \\frac{31}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{31M}{35}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{31M}{35}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{31}{35}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387481 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387482 13194139536178 true] [17592186387481 1089 "q-163609" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387481 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536178 true] [17592186387481 1100 "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the lines $y=3x,$ $x=1,$ $x=2,$ and the $x$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{45}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}).$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." 13194139536178 true] [17592186387481 1113 #uuid "a92867f4-65f2-5f14-8d1b-a73c2c61438b" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387481 1145 "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3x}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3x}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{M}{45}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{45}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3x}{x}^{4}+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{45}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{[{x}^{4}y+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{2}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{45}{\\int }_{1}^{2}3{x}^{5}+9{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{45}{\\int }_{1}^{2}12{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{45}[2{x}^{6}]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{45}\\cdot (128-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{14M}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387482 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387483 13194139536178 true] [17592186387482 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387484 13194139536178 true] [17592186387482 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387485 13194139536178 true] [17592186387482 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387486 13194139536178 true] [17592186387482 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387487 13194139536178 true] [17592186387482 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536178 true] [17592186387482 1041 "selection" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387482 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387484 13194139536178 true] [17592186387482 1110 #uuid "63126a26-4cf4-5c06-8d5b-6d0fa87cab70" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387483 1034 "2" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387483 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536178 true] [17592186387483 1111 #uuid "ffe23f76-cbf2-5ee1-888a-612dc11574c7" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387484 1034 "\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{5}}" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387484 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536178 true] [17592186387484 1111 #uuid "4b73c887-8008-5c50-ac7e-765248ee1aa8" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387485 1034 "3\\sqrt{5}" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387485 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536178 true] [17592186387485 1111 #uuid "eff6ed9c-6392-5931-83e1-5eb23d43e9df" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387486 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387486 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536178 true] [17592186387486 1111 #uuid "0c1294f3-f321-5ce1-a4b5-ac0dca8a6fb6" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387487 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{2}" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387487 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536178 true] [17592186387487 1111 #uuid "682c55f5-e898-5089-86bf-316b20186aea" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387488 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387489 13194139536178 true] [17592186387488 1089 "q-163613" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387488 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536178 true] [17592186387488 1100 "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ bounded by the curve $y={x}^{3},$ the line $y=1,$ and the $y$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{28M}{3}x{y}^{3}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $x$-axis." 13194139536178 true] [17592186387488 1113 #uuid "ffd0f3a8-7727-507f-bb77-2d0f3f5f20c8" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387488 1145 "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{1}{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{28M}{3}x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{28M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{1}x{y}^{5}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{28M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{6}x{y}^{6}]}_{y={x}^{3}}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x-{x}^{19}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{9}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{20}{x}^{20}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{9}(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{20}) \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{9}\\cdot \\frac{9}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{x} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{7M}{10}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{10}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387489 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387490 13194139536178 true] [17592186387489 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387491 13194139536178 true] [17592186387489 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387492 13194139536178 true] [17592186387489 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387493 13194139536178 true] [17592186387489 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387494 13194139536178 true] [17592186387489 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536178 true] [17592186387489 1041 "selection" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387489 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387491 13194139536178 true] [17592186387489 1110 #uuid "adc80f8e-86ac-5153-8a5b-c59d69c64f30" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387490 1034 "\\frac{9}{20}" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387490 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536178 true] [17592186387490 1111 #uuid "e0d0c944-2c09-571a-b932-6ac31ac42186" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387491 1034 "\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{10}}" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387491 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536178 true] [17592186387491 1111 #uuid "bcc92b23-4af0-52da-b897-4638f865fb77" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387492 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{7}" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387492 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536178 true] [17592186387492 1111 #uuid "67ef8e6d-f2f7-5138-befa-944c6d81e56f" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387493 1034 "\\frac{5}{8}" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387493 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536178 true] [17592186387493 1111 #uuid "a101f896-83d8-5acc-833c-86cd9e9bd1e2" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387494 1034 "\\sqrt{\\frac{11}{20}}" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387494 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536178 true] [17592186387494 1111 #uuid "b1fdf91d-9317-5c37-897f-9ce20e389d68" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387495 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387496 13194139536178 true] [17592186387495 1089 "q-163654" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387495 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536178 true] [17592186387495 1100 "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 6.$ Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{9\\pi }{y}^{2}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." 13194139536178 true] [17592186387495 1113 #uuid "e271defa-4e74-5933-b22e-63a7dc60b0bc" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387495 1145 "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{6},\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{M}{9\\pi }{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{6}}{r}^{5}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9\\pi }({\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{6}}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}{r}^{6}{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{6}}({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9\\pi }\\cdot 36\\cdot {[\\frac{\\theta }{2}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }{4}]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9\\pi }\\cdot 36\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =4M.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{0} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4M\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387496 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387497 13194139536178 true] [17592186387496 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387498 13194139536178 true] [17592186387496 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387499 13194139536178 true] [17592186387496 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387500 13194139536178 true] [17592186387496 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387501 13194139536178 true] [17592186387496 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536178 true] [17592186387496 1041 "selection" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387496 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387499 13194139536178 true] [17592186387496 1110 #uuid "46a5a9ba-52e0-5f87-9e22-f07a2471d91e" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387497 1034 "\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{2}}" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387497 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536178 true] [17592186387497 1111 #uuid "70ca94a1-c5e0-5434-94ce-6e1a4e93a5c0" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387498 1034 "3" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387498 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536178 true] [17592186387498 1111 #uuid "7639758c-e2bd-596b-be95-b27cff889761" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387499 1034 "2" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387499 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536178 true] [17592186387499 1111 #uuid "4fc223e1-2b2d-5ff1-a100-c3dad383b958" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387500 1034 "\\sqrt{6}" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387500 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536178 true] [17592186387500 1111 #uuid "f6e243d3-87ac-59be-b10d-d8e8bf871444" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387501 1034 "\\frac{7}{3}" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387501 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536178 true] [17592186387501 1111 #uuid "6e6b12e3-d3d4-5fce-9a97-a9d020630dd6" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387502 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387503 13194139536178 true] [17592186387502 1089 "q-163658" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387502 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536178 true] [17592186387502 1100 "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=3.$ Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{2}{9\\pi }M({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}).$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." 13194139536178 true] [17592186387502 1113 #uuid "72ac20b5-e801-55d9-abc7-3c66cee0c8b5" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387502 1145 "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{3},\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{2}{9\\pi }M{r}^{2}.$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9\\pi }M{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}{r}^{5}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9\\pi }M({\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9\\pi }M\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}{r}^{6}{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9\\pi }M\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{\\theta }{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }{4}]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{\\pi }\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =M.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{M\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387503 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387504 13194139536178 true] [17592186387503 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387505 13194139536178 true] [17592186387503 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387506 13194139536178 true] [17592186387503 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387507 13194139536178 true] [17592186387503 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387508 13194139536178 true] [17592186387503 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536178 true] [17592186387503 1041 "selection" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387503 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387507 13194139536178 true] [17592186387503 1110 #uuid "d11cce61-8a3e-51f8-833e-4f95978d8350" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387504 1034 "\\sqrt{2}" 13194139536178 true] [17592186387504 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536178 true] [17592186387504 1111 #uuid "92328e91-502e-5c01-8430-d0